  "body": "## Change\n\nAllow a setup-session acknowledgment for a single upright setup that uses model stock marked as raw stock only. Compare the incoming and finished stock on the same simulation grid. Report the count, maximum depth and location of deficient cells that stay at their incoming heights. A new or deeper deficit still holds posting.\n\nOpening the project clears the acknowledgment and keeps the raw-stock-only mark. The MCP tool `set_raw_stock_only` exposes the optional acknowledgment (`report_inherited_deficits`).\n\n### Review fixes (`3c4e3b7b8`)\n\nTwo independent reviews of the first version found six cases. Each case has a pinning test that fails without its fix.\n\n- A program of touch probes only plans nothing in the column simulation (#108). It was refused even with the acknowledgment. Now it is judged and noted the same way.\n- A torch or a wire removes material that the column never sees (#670). An undercut pass lowers no column top (#1444). A program with one of these keeps the full gate, because unchanged tops cannot show that the program left a cell alone.\n- A probe in a setup other than the judged one never uses that setup's acknowledgment.\n- A program that cuts nothing was judged on the first setup's stock, wherever it ran. Now `carry::walk` takes its steps from the program's own operations when nothing is planned. The program is judged on the setup it runs in and crosses setups by the same entry law as a cutting program. Cutting programs walk exactly as before. **This changes the ordinary verdict (acknowledgment off) for programs of probes or torches only.**\n- Across setups that the walk cannot cross (a later setup's model stock, a machine change), such a program now refuses by name in the not-judged arm. Before, it posted. The operations' generator verdicts judge paths, not stock.\n\n## Readings\n\nThe synthetic fixture has a step 5 mm below the part surface. Posting holds before acknowledgment, passes with a located 5.00 mm note after acknowledgment, and holds again after reopening. A second cut that deepens the step by 3 mm still holds posting. A probe-only program behaves the same way on the stock of its own setup. A torch, a T-slot pass, or a probe in another setup keeps the hold. A two-setup probe or plasma program that the walk cannot cross is refused, and no NC file is written.\n\n## Checks\n\n- On `3c4e3b7b8`, `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` passed 353 of 354 steps, with 0 stalled. The one failure was the golden comparison in `sinumerik_810m_post`. It read a stale CRLF working copy of the committed kit file `docs/tester-kits/sinumerik-810m-vmc200/air_cut_vmc200.mpf`, which is marked `eol=lf` and is not changed by this PR. After the copy was restored to the committed bytes (no diff), that suite passed 3 of 3.\n- Clippy passed for all targets of `camcraft-app` with warnings denied.\n- The 16 pinning tests are in the `keep_law` binary under `incoming_stock_deficits`. Twenty other suites on posting, probing, plasma and setups also passed: 179 of 179 tests in 21 suites on `3c4e3b7b8`.\n\nThe test setup uses synthetic stock on Windows. The light lane belongs to the independent upstream review. Full heavy lanes run at the release cut.\n\nThe fork synced at v0.26.0.\n\nEffort: high\n\nChangelog: Report acknowledged incoming-stock deficits that the program leaves at their incoming heights; judge a probe- or torch-only program on the setup it runs in.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nFixes #4056\n",
